## Canonical outputs and retirement successor

Only `plan.json`, `cards/CLK-06.md` and new `evidence/CLK-06.json` are written.
The plan is not wholly reserialized: only the CLK-06 task's raw JSON span is
replaced. All other63 raw task-object bytes and parsed semantics are checked
unchanged. The card's four checkboxes close and Root's approved notes append.
Korean status strings use Unicode escapes; notes/card bytes are decoded UTF8.
No generic Rust500-line rule or fabricated line count is imposed.

Completion evidence schema is `clk06-card-completion-evidence.v1`, with direct
`unit.report`/`production.report`, their real execution/review refs and actual
comparison counts, `actual_final_quality`, `applied_core_inventory`, contracts,
archive/verification refs, preserved failures and explicit unpaired scope.

Actual stdout/result schema is `clk06-metadata-card-closure.v1`: `before`2,
`after`3, `previously_absent_evidence`, `only_CLK06_gates_updated:true`,
`other_63_tasks_unchanged:true`, `other_63_raw_task_object_bytes_unchanged:true`,
actual quality/archive refs and source copies. `archived_deltas` holds exact
`{path,before,after}` byte archives of plan/card so later retirement can prove
scope.after -> closure.before -> closure.after without requiring the old pending
plan to remain live. HTML/view synchronization, Git publication and retirement
are separate Root actions; this writer performs none of them.
